market tests
A Python framework for backtesting and benchmarking intra (and infra) day trading strategies against historical market data. Built to test trend-following and momentum models against a buy and hold baseline.
Conclusion: All models tested do not yield better results than following market average.


Features

Execution Simulation: Tracks positions, PnL, trailing stops, and drawdowns.

compare.py runs multiple strategy variations head-to-head on identical data.
main.py for Application entry point.

GUI Dashboard: PyQt interface (dashboard.py) for visual backtest playback.


Structure
feed.py — Data feed handler fetching historical price series via yfinance.
strategy.py — Quantitative strategy definitions (SimpleMomentumStrategy, FilteredTrendStrategy).
engine.py — Order execution, position management, and PnL tracking.
compare.py — Benchmarking script to compare strategies side-by-side.
dashboard.py — PyQt visual playback interface.


